.TH "SPEECHSYNTHESISUTTERANCE.RESUME_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SpeechSynthesisUtterance.resume_event \- SpeechSynthesisUtterance:
resume event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]resume\f[B]\f[R] event of the Web Speech API
\f[CR]SpeechSynthesisUtterance\f[R] object is fired when a paused
utterance is resumed.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqresume\(dq, (event) => { })

onresume = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]SpeechSynthesisEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
You can use the \f[CR]resume\f[R] event in an
\f[CR]addEventListener\f[R] method:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.addEventListener(\(dqresume\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaSpeech resumed after ${event.elapsedTime} seconds.\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Or use the \f[CR]onresume\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.onresume = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaSpeech resumed after ${event.elapsedTime} seconds.\(ga);
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Web Speech API
